86342015 13194139535290 true] [17592186342014 1089 "q-127049" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342014 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535290 true] [17592186342014 1100 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=2{x}^{2}\\,i+2{y}^{2}\\,j$ and the circle $C$ given by ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$ If the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: The outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C$ is $n=\\frac{x}{2}\\,i+\\frac{y}{2}\\,j.$*" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342014 1113 #uuid "cc107592-3a31-505e-b22b-e74c3d756b36" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342014 1145 "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061989/assets/ff84680c55f5349431cf3d70066eeaba2c680569faa3b2210e5d14ef63ccd99e.png)\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}(2{x}^{2}\\,i+2{y}^{2}\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{x}{2}i+\\frac{y}{2}\\,j)\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is ${x}^{3}+{y}^{3}.$" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342016 13194139535290 true] [17592186342015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342017 13194139535290 true] [17592186342015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342018 13194139535290 true] [17592186342015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342019 13194139535290 true] [17592186342015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342020 13194139535290 true] [17592186342015 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535290 true] [17592186342015 1041 "selection" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342015 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342018 13194139535290 true] [17592186342015 1110 #uuid "54d2a749-f5dc-5d22-a107-bfd03b701359" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342016 1034 "{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342016 1111 #uuid "817eaed9-aac7-54b8-9d58-46629a352db4" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342017 1034 "{x}^{4}{y}^{4}" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342017 1111 #uuid "22d4f0cd-20ce-55c9-b00b-7d768b392fe0" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342018 1034 "{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342018 1111 #uuid "a9e4cdce-6d60-5d27-8767-09840e554cf3" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342019 1034 "x+y" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342019 1111 #uuid "19c86fc1-b324-5592-ac46-77db91ca2ee4" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342020 1034 "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342020 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342020 1111 #uuid "1ada45af-adf9-5687-9059-47a48e42de1b" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342021 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342022 13194139535290 true] [17592186342021 1089 "q-127050" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342021 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535290 true] [17592186342021 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061989/assets/4f8af75aece2346ffbf7a09e1ee90b6e0270f5661dd74e068abb2b2a848e5b97.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)={x}^{3}\\,i+3{y}^{2}\\,j$ and the square $C$ with side length $4$ centered at $O,$ shown above. If the flux of $F$ across the side ${C}_{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342021 1113 #uuid "83f77d00-0a21-52bf-87bb-6b8cfabd19ec" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342021 1145 "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nIn our case, we need to find an expression for the flux across only the part ${C}_{2}$ of the closed curve $C.$ Since this side is perpendicular to the $y$-axis and we require an outward-pointing unit normal vector, we must have $n=j.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061989/assets/a83c3476bbe2ed2872ed8938dda59c5d0e6d58d05ecaf662748e7a184a4994a4.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}({x}^{3}\\,i+3{y}^{2}\\,j)\\cdot j\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $3{y}^{2}.$" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342023 13194139535290 true] [17592186342022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342024 13194139535290 true] [17592186342022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342025 13194139535290 true] [17592186342022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342026 13194139535290 true] [17592186342022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342027 13194139535290 true] [17592186342022 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535290 true] [17592186342022 1041 "selection" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342022 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342025 13194139535290 true] [17592186342022 1110 #uuid "6b421dd2-7ae8-564d-ac09-6817620f6879" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342023 1034 "{x}^{3}{y}^{2}" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342023 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342023 1111 #uuid "1215f098-5fc4-5218-bfa9-e557b501fe00" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342024 1034 "{x}^{3}" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342024 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342024 1111 #uuid "09c40e3a-d109-5e20-a1d5-8e396d0bbd9a" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342025 1034 "3{y}^{2}" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342025 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342025 1111 #uuid "ed28d01f-bc38-5d9d-9163-725ce9fe3081" 13194139535290 true] [