rac{x}{2}\\,i+\\frac{y}{2}\\,j.$*" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342035 1113 #uuid "05a5811d-d732-5c24-84a4-d070b12f61bc" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342035 1145 "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061989/assets/ff84680c55f5349431cf3d70066eeaba2c680569faa3b2210e5d14ef63ccd99e.png)\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}(4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,i+2{x}^{3}y\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{x}{2}i+\\frac{y}{2}\\,j)\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}3{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $3{x}^{3}{y}^{2}.$" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342037 13194139535290 true] [17592186342036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342038 13194139535290 true] [17592186342036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342039 13194139535290 true] [17592186342036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342040 13194139535290 true] [17592186342036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342041 13194139535290 true] [17592186342036 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535290 true] [17592186342036 1041 "selection" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342036 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342038 13194139535290 true] [17592186342036 1110 #uuid "27171527-c232-535a-8f48-2fe7e205416c" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342037 1034 "3x+{y}^{3}" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342037 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342037 1111 #uuid "07a704fa-ec5c-59db-9f0a-6a4c76554cba" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342038 1034 "3{x}^{3}{y}^{2}" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342038 1111 #uuid "91883fcb-92cf-51cf-9272-6a3d73347fb9" 13194139535290 true] [1759218634