c430cadcc39c3d808001b2fd27665e968.png)\n\nNow, since the vector field $F=3\\,i$ is parallel to ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{4},$ there is zero net flow through these two sides. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{4}}F\\cdot {n}_{4}\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\nSo, our expression for the flux reduces to\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nNow, since the vector field is uniform, the net outflow through ${C}_{1}$ will cancel with the net inflow through ${C}_{3}.$ That is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s=-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s\\,⟹\\,{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342044 13194139535290 true] [17592186342043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342045 13194139535290 true] [17592186342043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342046 13194139535290 true] [17592186342043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342047 13194139535290 true] [17592186342043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342048 13194139535290 true] [17592186342043 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535290 true] [17592186342043 1041 "selection" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342043 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342047 13194139535290 true] [17592186342043 1110 #uuid "8a097576-867a-513a-ba36-bdfa1aa51298" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342044 1034 "2" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342044 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342044 1111 #uuid "34f6aa75-391e-5406-8a9f-7db3a0a58c42" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342045 1034 "-4" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342045 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342045 1111 #uuid "e544a02e-eaa4-5e72-9519-ef5a8265fbcb" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342046 1034 "4" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342046 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045