_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{4}}F\\cdot {n}_{4}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere the sides ${C}_{i}$ and unit vectors ${n}_{i}$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061989/assets/29f4b57751e27f01539fb48acf115b6e255d47a04ee647ef85aa496731b266c8.png)\n\nWe compute this integral in two stages. \n\n- First, consider the side ${C}_{1}.$ We have that ${n}_{1}=i,$ and therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}(-2x\\,i+5y\\,j)\\cdot i\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}x\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a line integral with respect to arc length, which we can evaluate in the usual way. Parameterizing the side ${C}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\nr(t)=i+t\\,j,\\,⇒\\,{r}^{′}(t)=j,\\,t\\in [-2,2].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}x\\,\\text{d}s & =-2{\\int }_{-2}^{2}1\\cdot ||{r}^{′}(t)||\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy symmetry, the flux integral across the side ${C}_{3}$ must be the same. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s=-8.\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider the side ${C}_{2}.$ We have that ${n}_{2}=j,$ and therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}(-2x\\,i+5y\\,j)\\cdot j\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}y\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a line integral with respect to arc length, which we can evaluate in the usual way. Parameterizing the side ${C}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nr(t)=t\\,i+2\\,j,\\,⇒\\,{r}^{′}(t)=i,\\,t\\in [-1,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}y\\,\\text{d}s & =5{\\int }_{-1}^{1}2\\cdot ||{r}^{′}(t)||\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =10{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =10\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy symmetry, the flux integral across the side ${C}_{4}$ must be the same. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{4}}F\\cdot {n}_{4}\\,\\text{d}s=20.\n$$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=2\\cdot (-8)+2\\cdot 20=24.\n$$" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342093 13194139535290 true] [17592186342092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342094 13194139535290 true] [17592186342092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342095 13194139535290 true] [17592186342092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342096 13194139535290 true] [17592186342092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342097 13194139535290 true] [17592186342092 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535290 true] [17592186342092 1041 "selection" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342092 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342097 13194139535290 true] [17592186342092 1110 #uuid "7e6c0fc5-5b26-5950-a0d6-6c4f085b20d7" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342093 1034 "40" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342093 1111 #uuid "590066e2-34f7-5a51-bf80-f7a40f119dc8" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342094 1034 "36" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342094 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342094 1111 #uuid "507a2a13-b87a-5138-9332-cec9774b14ab" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342095 1034 "32" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342095 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342095 1111 #uuid "51e1872e-3feb-5ce6-a2aa-8a41c77ed404" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342096 1034 "48" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342096 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342096 1111 #uuid "dd2c657a-8284-5ac0-a027-35a216842f6c" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342097 1034 "24" 13194139535290 true] [17592186342097 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535290 true] [17592186342097 1111 #uuid "ee49900b-a164-58a6-b1bf-958719eefb8a" 13194139535290 true]] :edb/tempids {